 "what_landed": "champions/stat_ramp.py: a stack level whose grant no swing walker can carry, served as the level's time-weighted mean over the fight. Zaahen, Graves and Wukong are on it.",
 "why": [
  "An attack-speed ramp re-rates the very stream that stacks it, one swing at a time. A ramp granting attack damage or resistances has no such seam, because the stat sheet is resolved once and every cast is priced against it. The mean is the reading, and it is the approximation Terminus' penetration already makes: a burst at second one is priced at a level the fight only reaches later, and a fight that ends early is priced above what its first casts met. The module states that rather than leaving it to be found.",
  "Over twenty seconds: Zaahen's attack damage 107 at no stacks, 121.8 ramped, 169.1 at a declared full twelve. Graves' armor 83 / 93.6 / 139. Wukong's 90.8 / 125.2 / 134.9. Every reading sits between the two ends.",
  "101 of the 106 leaves are Zaahen's, because his grant is attack damage and it reaches every number he prices. Graves moves 3 and Wukong 2: their grant is resistances, which changes what they take rather than what they deal, and the golden fights measure what they deal.",
  "Two floors are named in the source. Graves' dash TOWARD a champion banks two stacks where this walks one, and the setup cast schedule carries haste but not his pellet cooldown refund. Zaahen's cache spells a staged decay that this does not walk; each stack simply expires its own five seconds.",
  "No coupled leaf moves: no coupled roster holds any of the three."
 ],
